/*
 * QEMU machine: rehost-{{MODEL_LOWER}}   (mixed-architecture chain)
 *
 * Generated by sboot-rehost from templates/machine_mixed_arch.c.tmpl. Honest model -
 * see 06_machine/bypasses.md.
 *
 * STRUCTURE ONLY. This file carries no chip constant: every address, offset, register
 * value and vendor string below is a {{PLACEHOLDER}} to be filled from STATIC.md and
 * stage_map.json (v2) - never borrowed from a reference example, never guessed. A value
 * that is not derived yet stays a comment ("undetermined - confirmed at step N"), not a
 * plausible number (CLAUDE.md section 7 rule 4). A reference example under examples/
 * shows what a filled machine looked like for ONE device; its values are not borrowable.
 *
 * Chain shape this skeleton fits: AArch32 boot stages on one CPU (cpu[CPU_BOOT]) that
 * ask for a warm reset into AArch64; the AArch64 CPU (cpu[CPU_MONITOR]) then runs the
 * EL3 monitor and everything after it. Everything after the first stage is reached by
 * the firmware's own code: this machine never loads a kernel, a DTB or a ramdisk. A
 * chain of another shape (AArch64 first, AArch32 later) needs the CPU and handoff
 * sections reworked - undetermined, no derived example covers it.
 *
 * Required QEMU core patch: scripts/patch_qemu_core.py --family mediatek (lets TCG
 * create an AArch32 CPU: aarch64=false). Build applies it; qemu_tree.sh reset undoes it.
 *
 * Run with single-threaded TCG (-accel tcg,thread=single): that is how the one
 * hand-made reference ran. Whether multi-threaded TCG is safe for the handoff watcher
 * and the patch tick below is unverified.
 *
 * Derived premises (STATIC.md / stage_map.json v2 - never borrowed):
 *   stages           {{STAGE_SUMMARY}}
 *   first entry PC   {{FIRST_ENTRY_PC}}   (stages[0].entry_pc, absolute; a Thumb entry carries bit 0)
 *   monitor CPU      {{CPU64_TYPE}}   (runs the EL3 monitor; created FIRST)
 *   boot CPU         {{CPU32_TYPE}}   (aarch64=false)
 *   interrupt ctrl   GICv{{GIC_REVISION}}, {{GIC_NUM_IRQ}} interrupt ids
 *   boot medium      {{HCI_KIND}} @ {{HCI_BASE}}
 *
 * Conventions:
 *  - Host diagnostics (info_report / warn_report / error_report -> stderr -> host_<N>.txt)
 *    are the machine's own words and never guest evidence. Nothing here prints to the
 *    guest console except uart_write(): a console line either came from firmware or it
 *    is not evidence. No function fills the UART receive buffer except the chardev
 *    callback (input comes from the harness outside QEMU).
 *  - Every site that differs from the real device (table row, hook, patch, injected
 *    value) carries a trailing comment tag of the form  bypass:<id>  where <id> is the
 *    "#<id>" heading of its entry in 06_machine/bypasses.md. One row, one entry; the
 *    entry has the four fields (target, reason, method, side effect) and a side effect
 *    that is empty or "no record" is invalid.
 *  - g_post_handoff is first-class: a register whose meaning differs before and after
 *    the warm reset into AArch64 consults it, and every such site cites its bypass id.
 *  - STATIC.md "address windows" table. Every window this machine opens, every read
 *    override and every injected or assumed value is one row of a table with that heading
 *    in STATIC.md (appended, never overwritten). The classifier and the fixers read that
 *    table, not this source, so a fact only in this file reaches nobody. Columns:
 *      base, size, name,
 *      source    dtb | disasm | observed | assumed,
 *      model     shadow | override | dedicated | catchall,
 *      phase     pre_handoff | post_handoff | both,
 *      kind      M | V | S,
 *      evidence  the disassembled function, the log line or the device-tree node,
 *      bypass    the "#<id>" of its ledger entry (empty for a window modelled faithfully),
 *      security_effect  true when the firmware reads the value on a signature-verification
 *                path (fuse, life cycle, lock state); false otherwise.
 *    One row per shadow_specs row, per rehost_add_dedicated call, per read_overrides row
 *    and reg_hooks row (it shares the bypass id of its source tag), and per value that is
 *    assumed instead of derived (the vector page, the first stage's RAM size).
 */

